Four of five checks is a workflow checklist, not a general accuracy percentage. The corrected artifact is exactly right; the complete workflow is unfinished. Untested agents receive no failure score. No relative speed, reliability, quality, or cost-per-success ranking is justified by these observations.

Total estimate across both Claude attempts: $0.286748. Provider invoices have not been reconciled. The explicit repair attempt counts as an additional attempt; neither attempt automatically retried API calls. The comparison is restricted to this one synthetic desktop CSV task, not the earlier GitHub/browser tasks.

## Article-ready note

In the desktop test, Claude used its native computer tool to open a CSV in LibreOffice Calc, correct two misspelled status values, and save a separate file. A read-only check confirmed that the saved CSV was correct and the source file was unchanged. The full task remained incomplete: a token-count request timed out while Claude was trying to reopen the saved file for verification. An earlier attempt had stopped because of a harness protocol error; both attempts are retained and together account for approximately $0.287 in estimated API usage. OpenAI was paused before execution because exposed credentials needed rotation, while Sai's desktop-control preflight returned an authorization error. These are incomplete test results, not grounds for ranking the three agents.
